Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 23:36:27 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 353/638] cdm: retain key-system updates for the AROS observer

Compile the generic key-system support observer on AROS so Chrome's renderer callback has its concrete provider. Unsupported key systems still report as an empty capability set.

AI_PHASE: chromium-shared-cef

AI_STATUS: exact-native-link-gap-fixed-under-validation

AI_VALIDATION: mixed-provenance diagnostic native link contained exactly one unresolved cdm::GetSupportedKeySystemsUpdates symbol

AI_ASSUMPTION: an empty unsupported-CDM result is a first-class non-error state on AROS

AI_LIMITATIONS: coherent archive rebuild, native relink, and encrypted-media behavior remain pending

AI_EVIDENCE: aros-opal-hosted-clean/test-artifacts/-cef-native-link-pass2-20260725/03-undefined-symbols.txt

AI_DECISION_CHAIN:
---
 components/cdm/renderer/BUILD.gn | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/components/cdm/renderer/BUILD.gn b/components/cdm/renderer/BUILD.gn
index 10ebce2eee..fe7a4e7cf3 100644
--- a/components/cdm/renderer/BUILD.gn
+++ b/components/cdm/renderer/BUILD.gn
@@ -17,7 +17,7 @@ static_library("renderer") {
     "//third_party/widevine/cdm:buildflags",
   ]
 
-  if (enable_library_cdms || is_win || is_android) {
+  if (enable_library_cdms || is_win || is_android || is_aros) {
     sources += [
       "key_system_support_update.cc",
       "key_system_support_update.h",
